<title>GERMANY: Six German institutes detail forecasts by region.</title>
<headline>Six German institutes detail forecasts by region.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The six leading German economic research institutes made the following forecasts in their semiannual report, which was obtained by Reuters early on Tuesday:</p>
<p>				     1997	1996	  1995</p>
<p>PAN-GERMANY</p>
<p> GDP growth in pct (real)     2.5	 1.5	   1.9</p>
<p> Unemployed (millions)	  4.000     3.945	 3.612</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		10.4	10.3	  9.4</p>
<p> Consumer price inflation     1.5	 1.5	   1.8</p>
<p>WEST GERMANY</p>
<p> GDP growth in pct (real)     2.5	 1.5	   1.6</p>
<p> Unemployed (millions)	  2.800     2.785	 2.565</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		9.0	 9.0	   8.3</p>
<p> Consumer price inflation     1.5	 1.5	   1.7</p>
<p>EAST GERMANY</p>
<p> GDP growth in pct (real)     2.0	 2.0	   5.3</p>
<p> Unemployed (millions)	  1.200     1.160	 1.047</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		16.0	15.5	  14.1</p>
<p> Consumer price inflation     1.5	 2.5	   2.1</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
